  service_history: Ryūhō (龍鳳; "Dragon Phoenix") was a light aircraft carrier of the
    Imperial Japanese Navy. She was converted from the submarine tender Taigei (大鯨;
    "Big Whale"), which had been used in the Second Sino-Japanese War. One of the
    least successful of the light aircraft carrier conversions due to her small size,
    slow speed and weak construction, during World War II, Ryūhō was used primarily
    as an aircraft transport and for training purposes, although she was also involved
